WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.680
Around 1077, in an abbey in Normandy,
a monk named Anselm wrote a prayer.

2
00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:11.300
Inside was an argument for God
that needs no observation at all.

3
00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:15.570
He began with a line from the Psalms:
the fool has said in his heart,

4
00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:17.400
there is no God.

5
00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:21.680
Anselm's point: even the
fool understands the word.

6
00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:26.710
So can you prove God exists just by
thinking carefully about what the word God

7
00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:27.850
means?

8
00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:31.660
In this mission, you'll follow
Anselm's argument step by step,

9
00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:33.850
from the mind to reality.

10
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:39.270
Then you'll see why Anselm thought God
cannot even be thought not to exist.

11
00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:44.430
Your mission: find out whether a definition
of God could prove that God exists.
